    "verdict": "No, not in the aggregate. At 4.2%, unemployment is at or below CBO's natural rate (4.4%), prime-age participation is above its pre-pandemic level, and its path tracks GDP growth about as Okun's law predicts. If AI-driven displacement is showing up, it is not yet in the headline rate. That is why the next sections look at who and where."
